+---
+id: task-005-add-createpatch-from-to-producing-a-minimal-rfc-6902-json-patch
+type: task
+title: "Add createPatch(from, to) producing a minimal RFC 6902 JSON Patch"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- task body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+## Request
+
+Export `createPatch(from, to)` from `src/index.ts`: returns an RFC 6902 JSON Patch that turns `from` into
+`to`, without mutating either input. The patch describes only what changed: small changes give small
+patches; array item insertions/removals give `add`/`remove` of that item; moves within an array give a
+move, or a remove plus an add, never a rewrite of the items in between.
+
+## Done
+
+Recursive diff of objects and arrays; arrays are aligned with a longest-common-subsequence, so
+inserted/removed/moved items are `add`/`remove` operations and changed items are patched in place.
+Tests in `test/createpatch.test.ts` (round trip through `applyPatch`, minimality, random round trips).
